# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Only the two files that are NOT fingerprinted get a Cache-Control rule.
# index.html and assets/config.js decide which bundle and which API the
# browser uses, so a cached copy serves a stale application or points at the
# wrong API. Everything else out of the Angular build carries a content hash,
# so a changed file is a changed URL and Pages' own defaults are correct for
# it — no broad Cache-Control rule here, deliberately, since two rules
# matching one path is how you end up unsure which one won.
#
# Consumed by Pages and never served.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

/assets/config.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
